{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791609549,"nonce":"7Pb5Y6+kNxYf6ngGvEmmahK2aUE=","message":"Decision (PM): replace the auto-detect-and-delete design. Paths resolve explicit setting then XDG default with no legacy fallback; an unmigrated data/jobhunter.db in the main checkout (git --git-common-dir, so worktrees map to it) or the cwd stops every command except paths, migrate-paths, init and schedule; both databases present without MOVED.txt is a conflict; jobhunter init for fresh installs. migrate-paths --apply refuses while the db is open (/proc scan plus a held exclusive sqlite lock), copies db/backups/cache/profile/resume, verifies integrity_check, schema, row counts and sha256, rolls back on failure, then renames the old folders to *.migrated-YYYYMMDD with MOVED.txt inside; no --remove-old. Reason: two reviews found the heuristic fallback and delete path forked or lost data. Supersedes decisions 3, 4 and 6.","files":null}]}